#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I cite Qiskit in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-qiskit-in-my-research}"
msgstr ""
"Comment citer Qiskit dans mes recherches ? {#how-do-i-cite-qiskit-in-my-"
"research}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cite Qiskit by using the included [BibTeX "
"file](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/CITATION.bib).\n"
msgstr ""
"Cite Qiskit en utilisant le [fichier "
"BibTeX](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/blob/main/CITATION.bib) fourni.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I cite an IBM Quantum computer in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-an-"
"ibm-quantum-computer-in-my-research}"
msgstr ""
"Comment citer un ordinateur IBM Quantum dans mes recherches ? {#how-do-i-"
"cite-an-ibm-quantum-computer-in-my-research}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For research papers, we encourage authors to acknowledge IBM Quantum&reg; by"
" using:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour les articles de recherche, nous encourageons les auteurs à mentionner "
"IBM Quantum&reg; en utilisant :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
">    We acknowledge the use of IBM Quantum services for this work. The views"
" expressed are those of the authors, and do not reflect the official policy "
"or position of IBM or the IBM Quantum team.\n"
msgstr ""
">    Nous reconnaissons l'utilisation des services IBM Quantum pour ce "
"travail. Les opinions exprimées sont celles des auteurs et ne reflètent pas "
"la politique officielle ou la position d'IBM ou de l'équipe IBM Quantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Paper references should use the following citation:\n"
msgstr ""
"Les références bibliographiques doivent utiliser la citation suivante :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> IBM Quantum. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/, YYYY\n"
msgstr "> IBM Quantum. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/, YYYY\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum processing units in the paper should be referenced by their unique name (for example, `ibmq_vigo`) and optionally\n"
"adding the version (for example, `ibmq_vigo` v1.0.2).  We also encourage referencing the processor.\n"
"For example:\n"
msgstr ""
"Les unités de traitement quantique dans l'article doivent être référencées par leur nom unique (par exemple, `ibmq_vigo`) en ajoutant éventuellement la version (par exemple, `ibmq_vigo` v1.0.2). Nous encourageons également à référencer le processeur.\n"
"Par exemple :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> In this paper we used `ibmq_vigo`, which is one of the IBM Quantum Canary "
"processors.\n"
msgstr ""
"> Dans cet article, nous avons utilisé `ibmq_vigo`, qui est l'un des "
"processeurs IBM Quantum Canary.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example of citing an IBM Quantum program:\n"
msgstr "Exemple de citation d'un programme IBM Quantum :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> IBM Quantum (2025). Estimator primitive (Version x.y.z) [computer "
"software]. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/\n"
msgstr ""
"> IBM Quantum (2025). Estimator primitive (Version x.y.z) [logiciel "
"informatique]. https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com</span>/\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I cite IBM Quantum Composer in my research? {#how-do-i-cite-ibm-"
"quantum-composer-in-my-research}"
msgstr ""
"Comment citer IBM Quantum Composer dans mes recherches ? {#how-do-i-cite-"
"ibm-quantum-composer-in-my-research}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example citation for IBM Quantum Composer:\n"
msgstr "Exemple de citation pour IBM Quantum Composer :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> IBM Quantum Composer. 2025. url: "
"https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer</span>\n"
msgstr ""
"> IBM Quantum Composer. 2025. url : "
"https://<span>quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer</span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I don't see something in the user interface, such as my administration "
"tasks. {#i-dont-see-something-in-the-user-interface-such-as-my-"
"administration-tasks}"
msgstr ""
"Je ne vois pas quelque chose dans l'interface utilisateur, comme mes tâches "
"d'administration. {#i-dont-see-something-in-the-user-interface-such-as-my-"
"administration-tasks}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Try choosing a different account from the account switcher in the header of "
"the [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com) interface.\n"
msgstr ""
"Essaie de choisir un autre compte depuis le sélecteur de comptes dans l'en-"
"tête de l'interface [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I'm just using the Open Plan, but I had to put in my credit card.  Will I be"
" charged? {#im-just-using-the-open-plan-but-i-had-to-put-in-my-credit-card-"
"will-i-be-charged}"
msgstr ""
"J'utilise seulement le plan Open, mais j'ai dû entrer ma carte de crédit. "
"Vais-je être facturé(e) ? {#im-just-using-the-open-plan-but-i-had-to-put-in-"
"my-credit-card-will-i-be-charged}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You will not be charged unless you create a Pay-As-You-Go "
"[instance](/guides/instances) and use it to send workloads to QPUs. See "
"[Manage cost](/guides/manage-cost) for instructions to set a cost limit and "
"to learn about other ways to manage costs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tu ne seras pas facturé(e) à moins que tu ne crées une "
"[instance](/guides/instances) Pay-As-You-Go et que tu l'utilises pour "
"envoyer des charges de travail aux QPU. Consulte [Gérer les "
"coûts](/guides/manage-cost) pour obtenir des instructions sur la définition "
"d'une limite de coût et pour en savoir plus sur d'autres façons de gérer les"
" coûts.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What's the difference between an API key and an API token? {#whats-the-"
"difference-between-an-api-key-and-an-api-token}"
msgstr ""
"Quelle est la différence entre une clé API et un jeton API ? {#whats-the-"
"difference-between-an-api-key-and-an-api-token}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's no difference.  The terms API key and API token are used "
"interchangeably. You'll see both terms in the documentation because "
"different interfaces use different terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il n'y a aucune différence. Les termes clé API et jeton API sont utilisés de"
" façon interchangeable. Tu verras les deux termes dans la documentation, car"
" différentes interfaces emploient des termes différents.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bearer\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"bearer\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What's the difference between an API token and a bearer token? {#whats-the-"
"difference-between-an-api-token-and-a-bearer-token}"
msgstr ""
"Quelle est la différence entre un jeton API et un jeton bearer ? {#whats-"
"the-difference-between-an-api-token-and-a-bearer-token}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An API token is a long-lived credential used to [authenticate to the Qiskit "
"Runtime service](/guides/hello-world#install-and-authenticate).  A bearer "
"token is a temporary credential that is used to [authenticate to the REST "
"API in an untrusted environment](/guides/cloud-setup-untrusted#authenticate-"
"to-the-rest-api-in-an-untrusted-environment).  A bearer token cannot be used"
" to authenticate to the Qiskit Runtime service.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un jeton API est un identifiant de longue durée utilisé pour [s'authentifier"
" auprès du service Qiskit Runtime](/guides/hello-world#install-and-"
"authenticate). Un jeton bearer est un identifiant temporaire utilisé pour "
"[s'authentifier auprès de l'API REST dans un environnement non "
"fiable](/guides/cloud-setup-untrusted#authenticate-to-the-rest-api-in-an-"
"untrusted-environment). Un jeton bearer ne peut pas être utilisé pour "
"s'authentifier auprès du service Qiskit Runtime.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Do I have to choose the region that I live in? {#do-i-have-to-choose-the-"
"region-that-i-live-in}"
msgstr ""
"Dois-je choisir la région dans laquelle je vis ? {#do-i-have-to-choose-the-"
"region-that-i-live-in}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No. You can use either region.  The region determines where jobs are run and"
" where the data is kept.  Additionally, you can only see and use instances "
"that were created in the instance that you are logged in to. Note that only "
"the us-east region supports the Open Plan.\n"
msgstr ""
"Non. Tu peux utiliser l'une ou l'autre des régions. La région détermine où "
"les jobs sont exécutés et où les données sont conservées. De plus, tu ne "
"peux voir et utiliser que les instances créées dans l'instance à laquelle tu"
" es connecté(e). Note que seule la région us-east prend en charge le plan "
"Open.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Can I connect through a proxy server? {#can-i-connect-through-a-proxy-"
"server}"
msgstr ""
"Puis-je me connecter via un serveur proxy ? {#can-i-connect-through-a-proxy-"
"server}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, but you must use Qiskit Runtime v0.44.0 or later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oui, mais tu dois utiliser Qiskit Runtime v0.44.0 ou une version "
"ultérieure.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What is the data retention policy? {#what-is-the-data-retention-policy}"
msgstr ""
"Quelle est la politique de conservation des données ? {#what-is-the-data-"
"retention-policy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM retains your (undeleted) job and usage data for three years while you "
"continue to use the Qiskit Runtime service.\n"
msgstr ""
"IBM conserve tes données de jobs et d'utilisation (non supprimées) pendant "
"trois ans tant que tu continues à utiliser le service Qiskit Runtime.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What happened to Python distributions such as Qiskit Aer, Qiskit Nature, and"
" Qiskit Experiments? {#what-happened-to-python-distributions-such-as-qiskit-"
"aer-qiskit-nature-and-qiskit-experiments}"
msgstr ""
"Qu'est-il arrivé aux distributions Python telles que Qiskit Aer, Qiskit "
"Nature et Qiskit Experiments ? {#what-happened-to-python-distributions-such-"
"as-qiskit-aer-qiskit-nature-and-qiskit-experiments}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, the command `pip install qiskit` "
"will **only** install the [Qiskit SDK](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit). "
"This means that some modules that you have used in the past, such as "
"`qiskit-aer` or `qiskit-nature`, now have to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr ""
"Depuis la sortie du Qiskit SDK v1.0, la commande `pip install qiskit` "
"n'installera **que** le [Qiskit SDK](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit). Cela"
" signifie que certains modules que tu as utilisés par le passé, tels que "
"`qiskit-aer` ou `qiskit-nature`, doivent désormais être installés "
"séparément.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit was comprised of many "
"different Python distributions, such as `qiskit-terra`, the compiler core; "
"`qiskit-aer`, the high-performance simulator; the original IBM Quantum&reg; "
"provider; and several now-obsolete packages providing particular exploratory"
" algorithmic or experiment-running features.\n"
msgstr ""
"Avant la sortie du Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit était composé de nombreuses "
"distributions Python différentes, telles que `qiskit-terra`, le cœur du "
"compilateur ; `qiskit-aer`, le simulateur haute performance ; le fournisseur"
" IBM Quantum&reg; d'origine ; et plusieurs packages désormais obsolètes "
"fournissant des fonctionnalités algorithmiques exploratoires particulières "
"ou d'exécution d'expériences.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These separate software packages were combined into what was called the "
"Qiskit *metapackage*, which allowed users to install all of these components"
" together through `pip install qiskit`. This metapackage architecture was "
"removed with the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, and now each of the "
"individual software distributions needs to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ces packages logiciels distincts ont été regroupés dans ce qu'on appelait le"
" *métapackage* Qiskit, qui permettait aux utilisateurs d'installer tous ces "
"composants ensemble via `pip install qiskit`. Cette architecture de "
"métapackage a été supprimée avec la sortie du Qiskit SDK v1.0, et chacune "
"des distributions logicielles individuelles doit maintenant être installée "
"séparément.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to install the packages that were previously included in the "
"Qiskit metapackage, visit the [Qiskit "
"ecosystem](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) to find a range of "
"packages to suit your needs. You can also read the [v1.0 migration "
"guide](/guides/metapackage-migration) for more information about this "
"change.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si tu veux installer les packages qui étaient précédemment inclus dans le "
"métapackage Qiskit, visite l'[écosystème "
"Qiskit](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) pour trouver une gamme de "
"packages adaptés à tes besoins. Tu peux également lire le [guide de "
"migration v1.0](/guides/metapackage-migration) pour plus d'informations sur "
"ce changement.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I close my IBM Cloud account? {#how-do-i-close-my-ibm-cloud-account}"
msgstr ""
"Comment fermer mon compte IBM Cloud ? {#how-do-i-close-my-ibm-cloud-account}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Find instructions on the [Closing an "
"account](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-account-close) "
"page.\n"
